## 1. Executive Summary & Business Problem

Traditional Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) systems depend on manual, rule-based processing, static historical moving averages, and "one-size-fits-all" forecasting. For electronics retailers facing rapid product evolution, this produces two critical supply chain failures, compounded by unmonitored supplier delivery delays:

- **Overstocking:** capital locked up in dead stock on slow-moving items.
- **Understocking:** micro-stockouts on high-velocity items.

**SmartPredict** is a decoupled, full-stack predictive ERP web application (`Python/Flask` backend + `React.js` frontend). It replaces static averages with an automated **Nodal Demand Framework** powered by **XGBoost** (`XGBRegressor`), **Exponential Moving Average (EMA) target denoising**, and **Coefficient of Variation (CV) supplier volatility scoring**. Complex ML metrics are translated into plain-English executive recommendations.

### Traditional ERP vs. SmartPredict

| Dimension | Traditional ERP | SmartPredict (AI-Enabled ERP) |
|---|---|---|
| Forecasting method | Static historical moving averages | XGBoost regressor trained per demand node |
| Product treatment | One-size-fits-all | Four demand nodes (Daily, Seasonal, Occasional, Top Selling), each with tailored features |
| Noise handling | Raw daily sales, sensitive to spikes | 7-day EMA denoised target (`Target_Trend`) |
| Accuracy reporting | Raw figures or none | WMAPE-based "Denoised Accuracy" with a plain-English justification |
| Supplier monitoring | Manual / unmonitored delays | Automated CV-based Supplier Volatility Score (0.60–0.96) |
| Inventory guidance | Manual report inputs | Automated action badges: `HOLD: Do Not Restock`, `OPTIMAL`, `CRITICAL` |
| Explainability | Raw data output | Feature-weight breakdown and written AI justifications in the UI |

---

## 2. Key Engineering Features

| Feature | What it does |
|---|---|
| **Nodal Demand Framework** | Classifies products into `Daily`, `Seasonal`, `Occasional` nodes (plus a `Top Selling` flag) and trains each with a node-specific feature set. |
| **EMA Target Denoising** | Forecasts a smoothed 7-day EMA baseline (`Target_Trend`) instead of raw daily sales, addressing "lazy prediction" (copying `Lag_1`). |
| **XGBoost 7-Day Forecasting** | Chronological 80/20 split, constrained trees (`max_depth=3`, `learning_rate=0.05`) to limit overfitting. |
| **Leakage Mitigation** | All rolling-window features are shifted by one day (`.shift(1)`), mitigating target leakage. |
| **WMAPE Evaluation** | Zero-safe accuracy metric suited to retail series with zero-sales days. |
| **CV Supplier Risk Engine** | Scores supplier delivery consistency from order-to-delivery lead-time variability. |
| **Explainable AI React Dashboard** | Login-gated SPA with three tabs: Executive Overview, AI Prediction, Supplier Analysis. |

---

## 3. System Architecture & Data Flow

```text
 ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │  RAW RELATIONAL ERP DATA (Maven Analytics)    │
 │  Sales.csv  Products.csv  Stores.csv          │
 │  Customers.csv         (ISO-8859-1 encoded)   │
 └───────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘
                         │
                         ▼
 ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │  preprocess.py   (ETL & Data Federation)      │
 │  • Joins on ProductKey / StoreKey / CustomerKey│
 │  • US-only + USD-only filtering               │
 │  • Median imputation (Square Meters, dates)   │
 │  • assign_node() demand categorisation        │
 └───────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘
                         │
                         ▼
 ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │  Federated_Electronics_Data.csv               │
 │  33,767 rows × 38 columns                     │
 └───────────┬───────────────────────┬───────────┘
             │                       │
             ▼                       ▼
 ┌─────────────────────────┐  ┌──────────────────────────────────┐
 │  model_training.py      │  │  app.py  (Flask REST API)        │
 │  Offline validation     │  │  • load_clean_data()             │
 │  • RMSE over 100 epochs │  │  • feature_engineering_and_      │
 │  • Training_Progress.png│  │    training()                    │
 │  • Feature_Importance.png│ │  • WMAPE accuracy                │
 └─────────────────────────┘  │  • CV supplier risk scoring      │
                              └────────────────┬─────────────────┘
                                               │  JSON over HTTP
                                               │  GET /api/dashboard-data?category=...
                                               ▼
                              ┌──────────────────────────────────┐
                              │  App.js  (React.js SPA)          │
                              │  http://localhost:3000           │
                              │  Login → Overview | AI Prediction│
                              │          | Supplier Analysis     │
                              └──────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Repository files**

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `Sales.csv`, `Products.csv`, `Stores.csv`, `Customers.csv` | Raw relational ERP datasets |
| `preprocess.py` | ETL and data federation; outputs `Federated_Electronics_Data.csv` |
| `Federated_Electronics_Data.csv` | Core federated dataset (33,767 rows × 38 columns) ingested by the backend |
| `model_training.py` | Offline training/validation; generates `Training_Progress.png` and `Feature_Importance.png` |
| `app.py` | Flask REST API at `http://127.0.0.1:5000`; forecasting, WMAPE, supplier risk |
| `App.js` | React.js SPA at `http://localhost:3000`; authentication and three dashboard tabs |

